    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. i'm looking at one specific piece right now and there's a pretty large knot right about halfway down the span, and some deep looking cracks running along the grain. i can't find a local engineer until monday tho. in the meantime, how do i actually judge if those internal cracks/knots make the beam unsafe or if they are just cosmetic? is there a way to tell if something is \"hiding\" deep in the wood that might cause it to fail later?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
