      "content": "fair enough, i'll wait for the engineer. it's just a bit unnerving knowing there could be something in there i can't see. like, when you talk about \"hidden defects\" that you can't see with your eyes, are you talking about actual structural voids or just density changes? i'm just trying to wrap my head around how something can be \"hiding\" inside a solid piece of timber and compromise the whole thing.",
